---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Security & privacy" description="How this site handles your data">
  <article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1>Security &amp; privacy</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      This site is fully static — no server, no database, no analytics that fingerprint you.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts, no sign-in, no cookies set by us.</li>
      <li>No analytics, no third-party trackers.</li>
      <li>No server logs of your requests (there's no server).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What your browser stores</h2>
    <p>
      Your color-theme choice is saved in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so it persists
      between visits. Nothing else is stored, and nothing is sent anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>How the data on this site is sourced</h2>
    <p>
      The CV body is hand-authored YAML in the
      <a href="https://github.com/CAM-eEng/CV">repo</a>. The activity visualizer snapshots GitHub
      and HackTheBox public data nightly via a build job.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting</h2>
    <p>
      Found something? Email <a href="mailto:ledge.valley8269@eagereverest.com"
        >ledge.valley8269@eagereverest.com</a
      >
      or open an issue on the public repo.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
